github.com/digitorus/pdf v0.1.2 — the ORIGINAL, for a test only
==================================================================

read.go, lex.go and text.go are copied unchanged from the Go module cache's github.com/digitorus/pdf@v0.1.2
(the three files the package's reader needs to compile; LICENSE is upstream's, BSD-style, The Go Authors).

Why: /pending 759. `FuzzThePatchedObjectStreamReaderMatchesTheOriginal` (internal/sign/objstmfuzz_test.go)
resolves the same random object streams through this original and through the patched copy in
third_party/digitorus-pdf (go.mod's replace target), and compares every value and every panic.

It never ships: it lives under testdata, which the go tool leaves out of `./...`, and only that test
imports it. `TestTheOriginalReaderCopyIsUpstreamUnchanged` fails when any of the three files differs from
the module cache's.
